    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d527">

                <pb facs="0639" n="629" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg629"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50/11–244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kennan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-02T09:00:00+03:00">November 2, 1944—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 12:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4194. ReEmbs 4001, October 20, 1 p.m. The British Ambassador has received a
                    letter from Vyshinski dated October 28 stating that the British proposal for the
                    establishment of an European Economic Committee had been referred to the
                    appropriate Soviet authorities <pb facs="0640" n="630" xml:id="pg630"/> for
                    study and requesting further information concerning the proposed tasks,
                    functions and structure of the committee.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
